    {
      "chunk": {
        "chunk_id": "guide-k8s-dependency-failures#fix-the-dependency-not-the-caller-1",
        "doc_path": "fixtures/knowledge-overlays/kubernetes/guide-k8s-dependency-failures.md",
        "title": "Guide: Kubernetes failures that come from a dependency",
        "heading": "Fix the dependency, not the caller",
        "text": "Rolling back or restarting a caller whose only problem is a failing dependency changes\nnothing, and it adds a second change to an incident that is already confusing. RECAP calls\nthis a dependency failure and never acts on it directly. Once the deepest failing service is\nknown, diagnose it with the matching runbook (a stalled rollout, a crash loop, readiness or\nmemory pressure) and fix that service.",
